  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nOften used in the pattern Xが{尽|つ}きる (X runs out). The negative form {尽|つ}きない and the pattern {尽|つ}きることなく (without running out) are common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {体力|たいりょく}が{尽|つ}きる — stamina runs out\n- {食料|しょくりょう}が{尽|つ}きる — food supply runs out\n- {忍耐|にんたい}が{尽|つ}きる — patience runs out\n- {話題|わだい}が{尽|つ}きない — topics never run out\n- {言葉|ことば}に{尽|つ}きない — beyond words, inexpressible\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\nなくなる is the everyday word for running out or disappearing. {尽|つ}きる is more literary and emphasizes complete exhaustion. {切|き}れる can also mean to run out (e.g., バッテリーが{切|き}れる) but focuses on breaking or disconnecting.",
